# 003 · No default spend limit for advisors

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

The advisors' daily spend limit (`max_usd_per_day`) has no default. A limit applies only when someone sets it.

## Why

No default caps is a rule for every goal. Before this goal, advisors stopped at 20 USD a day unless configured otherwise.

## Done when

- [x] `max_usd_per_day` is optional, and advisors apply it only when it is set. (`d2df6de`: `src/supervisor/advisors.ts`, `src/supervisor/advise.ts`)
- [x] A test shows that advisors run with no limit when none is set. (`d2df6de`: `src/supervisor/advisors.test.ts`; the advisors and advisor-routes tests pass, 10 of 10)
- [x] The settings docs say so. (`d2df6de`: `docs/local-development.md`)

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: No cap by default. Anyone who wants a limit can configure one.

## Open questions

None.

